//　…………撲殺していた。

//　いや。
//　殺してはいないのだろうが。

//　捉えた敵の目前で沈み込み、伸び上がりながら肝臓
//を抉る鉤打ちがまず初弾。
//　続いて左掌での側面張り手――鼓膜潰し。

//　奇怪な悲鳴を上げ、耳を押さえてのけぞる男の、胸
//に手を当て、同時に足をからめ、そして押し。

//　――男が仰向けに倒れる。
//　その、転倒の瞬間。
  Ichijo is beating a man to death.<K>
  At least, that's how I'm tempted to describe it.

  She comes in fast and low against her target, then springs up with a right hook that seems designed to tear the man's liver from his belly. She then follows with an open-handed slap to the side of the head, collapsing his eardrum.

  Her victim howls, clutching his ear. As he throws his head back, Ichijo seizes him by the collar, winds her left leg around his right, and pushes.

  The man topples backwards, and just as his back hits the floor―

//　胸板へ踵を打ち下ろした。
//　背と胸が共に、鈍い音を立てる。

//　男の口が最後に零した音声は、水袋を踏み潰す時の
//それに酷似していた。

//　……殺してはいないのだろうが。
//　充分に、殺人的な光景ではあった。

//　容赦の<RUBY text='かけら'>欠片</RUBY>もない。
//　致命打は与えないよう配慮したと<RUBY text='おぼ'>思</RUBY>しいが、それは
//容赦とは違う。

//　といって逆に、憤激に任せて暴力を振り回したのと
//も違う。
//　彼女は己の暴力を統制している。

//　でなければ、あんなにも<RUBY text='・・・'>綺麗に</RUBY>人を殴り倒せない。

//　……おそらく、一条は……
//　
//　俺は推測する。

//　鉄棒でスタッフらを殴り倒す覆面男を見た瞬間に。
//　胸中で裁判を行い、断罪し、与えるべき刑を決定し、
//それを執行したのだ。

//　ならばそこに容赦も加減も不要。
//　厳格なる執行の精神だけが求められる。

//　それが一条の戦いであり、戦い方。
//　そうではないのか。

//　――乱戦の中の一瞬。
//　俺は一条の本質に触れたのかもしれない。

//　――その一瞬。
//　俺は綾弥一条という人間を畏れた。
  She drops her heel hard against his sternum.

  A dull thud and sharp crack echo through the garage. The last sound that escapes the man's throat calls to mind air bladders being crushed at the fish market.

  She has not actually taken the man's life, but the sight is no less gruesome than if she had.

  There was no hint of mercy in her strikes. She took care not to do lethal damage, but that is not the same thing as mercy.

  Nor, however, did she strike out of uncontrolled rage. She clearly has a tight rein on her violence. Otherwise she would not be able to down a man so efficiently.

  Perhaps...<K> 
  An explanation dawns on me.

  The moment she entered the garage and saw masked men attacking the defenseless crew, she held tribunal in her mind, found them guilty, and passed sentence.

  All that remained, then, was to execute it. Mercy and moderation were not considerations. She needed only the resolve to mete out justice.

  That is Ichijo's fight. Her <I>Way.</I> 
  Or so it seems to me.

  ...In this moment, amidst the chaos, I catch what might be a glimpse of Ichijo's nature.

  And in this moment, I fear her.
